Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: gpio: apple,d2365-pmic-gpio: Add the D2186

The Dialog D2186 PMIC on A8 devices such as the iPod touch 6 (N102)
provides 21 GPIOs through the parent Apple I2C PMIC's regmap, driving
board signals such as Wi-Fi REG_ON and Bluetooth power enable.

Add its compatible. Its PMU event block is not wired yet, so like the
D2333 it is not an interrupt controller.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Berkay Kösebay <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Link: https://github.com/OrchardLinux/orchard/pull/231#issuecomment-7138590680
---
 .../bindings/gpio/apple,d2365-pmic-gpio.yaml          | 11 +++++++----
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/gpio/apple,d2365-pmic-gpio.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/gpio/apple,d2365-pmic-gpio.yaml
index 978a5a2..f1a4b21 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/gpio/apple,d2365-pmic-gpio.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/gpio/apple,d2365-pmic-gpio.yaml
@@ -10,9 +10,9 @@ maintainers:
   - Paul Praschl <praschlpaul@g-p.at>
 
 description: |
-  The Dialog D2207 PMIC used with the Apple A8X and the D2333 and D2365
-  PMICs used in Apple A9 and A10 devices provide 21, 21 and 24 GPIOs
-  respectively. The controller is accessed through the regmap exported by the
+  The Dialog D2186 and D2207 PMICs used with the Apple A8 and A8X and the
+  D2333 and D2365 PMICs used in Apple A9 and A10 devices provide 21, 21, 21
+  and 24 GPIOs respectively. The controller is accessed through the regmap exported by the
   parent Apple I2C PMIC device.
 
   The D2207 and D2365 also latch 112 and 240 PMU events respectively
@@ -34,6 +34,7 @@ description: |
 properties:
   compatible:
     enum:
+      - apple,d2186-pmic-gpio
       - apple,d2207-pmic-gpio
       - apple,d2333-pmic-gpio
       - apple,d2365-pmic-gpio
@@ -84,7 +85,9 @@ allOf:
   - if:
       properties:
         compatible:
-          const: apple,d2333-pmic-gpio
+          enum:
+            - apple,d2186-pmic-gpio
+            - apple,d2333-pmic-gpio
     then:
       properties:
         interrupt-controller: false
